=\frac{36}{\pi^3\,(r^2-2)}-\frac{8640}{\pi^3\,r^4}+\frac{18144}{\pi^3\,r^2}.\end{equation}
Therefore, the identity \eqref{eqn:a-another-integral} holds for $r>\sqrt{2}$.

